    "created_at": "2024-02-12T15:45:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-02-12T15:45:44Z",
    "body": "The legacy HTML fragment parser APIs don't support DSD and don't have Sanitizer API support. They also parse as HTML or XML depending on the \"[HTML document](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#html-document)\" bit on the document, and `setHTML()` and `setHTMLUnsafe()` always parse as HTML. (If we want XML variants in the future, we can add `setXMLUnsafe()` etc.) So possible axes are:\r\n\r\n- position\r\n- sanitize or not\r\n- HTML/XML\r\n\r\nI think option 1 is not a sufficient improvement to be worthwhile, it would still be a clunky API and it might be hard to add Sanitizer API in a consistent way.\r\n\r\nOption 3 would make existing methods XSS sinks.",
