    "created_at": "2025-09-18T12:53:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-09-18T12:53:48Z",
    "body": "See https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11669\nBasically suggesting to have `before` and `after` arguments when setting/streaming HTML, with splice-like semantics.\n\nThe issue with doing something specific to `insertAdjacentHTML`, is that while it is a nicer API in isolation, it means that we have to add a 3rd axis (safe/unsafe, streaming/direct, insert/replace) to the list of permutations, ending up with 8 methods... \nHaving a lot of separate methods to change HTML might be alright, but might also create more burden on linters and on explaining the platform. In the end it's a judgement call and we can come up with the balance that seems sensible and extend it later based on demand.",
